# PART 2 — PRODUCT DESIGN PRINCIPLES

Follow these principles throughout development.

1. Build real functionality, not decorative buttons.
2. Every dashboard metric must come from actual application data.
3. AI-generated conclusions must include explanations and evidence.
4. Never present guesses as verified facts.
5. Distinguish direct dependencies from inferred dependencies.
6. Show confidence levels for AI predictions.
7. Maintain a complete change history.
8. Protect the original project when running simulations.
9. Ensure users can understand technical results without being senior developers.
10. Design the platform for actual development teams, not just project demonstrations.

The platform must be modular, maintainable, scalable, testable, and secure.

