# PART 16 — STRICT DEVELOPMENT RULES

These rules are mandatory.

1. Never generate an entire application as disconnected sample pages.
2. Never create buttons that do nothing.
3. Never use fake analytics in real dashboard screens.
4. Never store important data only in browser state.
5. Never bypass backend authorization.
6. Never expose API keys.
7. Never trust AI-generated dependency relationships without validation.
8. Never modify real project data during hypothetical simulations.
9. Never claim that an integration works without testing it.
10. Never claim that an algorithm is predictive without measurable validation.
11. Never sacrifice security for convenience.
12. Never break existing working modules while adding new features.
13. Never use placeholder implementations in features marked complete.
14. Never hide errors from the user.
15. Always provide meaningful error messages.
16. Always validate API requests.
17. Always handle loading, empty, success, and failure states.
18. Always write tests for important algorithms and business logic.
19. Keep the implementation modular and maintainable.
20. Maintain a clear record of completed, pending, and partially implemented features.

