# PART 17 — DEFINITION OF DONE

A feature is complete only when:

- Its frontend interface exists.
- Its backend functionality exists.
- Its database integration works.
- Authentication and authorization are enforced.
- Input validation works.
- Error handling works.
- Loading and empty states work.
- Important business logic is tested.
- Its user journey works end to end.
- Documentation is updated.

A visually complete screen is not a completed feature.

A successful API response is not proof of a complete user workflow.

